<title>RUSSIA: Russian, Swedish firms launch Baltic ferry line.</title>
<headline>Russian, Swedish firms launch Baltic ferry line.</headline>
<dateline>ST.PETERSBURG 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A regular ferry service between St.Petersburg and the Swedish city of Oxelosund will be launched in April, a senior official of the Russian company AO Leningrad-Impex said on Friday.</p>
<p>Viktor Morozov, the company's chief of transport department, said that Swedish shipping company Nordic Trucker Line had leased a Gotland ferry for the four times a week service.</p>
<p>&quot;It has a capacity of 200 passengers and 140 cars and containers,&quot; Morozov said.</p>
<p>He said the project's cost was $50 million Swedish crowns ($6.7 million).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 85 20</p>
</text>
